---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="product-section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="product-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE EDITOR</p>
      <h2 id="demo-heading">Yes, that blue screen is real.</h2>
    </div>
    <figure class="product-figure">
      <div class="screenshot-frame"><img src="/images/turboj-editor.webp" width="1060" height="740" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="TurboJ Java editor showing Hello.java, compiler cache status, and successful Hello World execution in the integrated console." /></div>
      <figcaption><span>TurboJ running a Java Hello World program, with compiler status and execution output in the same window.</span><a href={site.links.original} data-testid="screenshot-original" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full resolution <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="product-copy">
      <p>TurboJ takes inspiration from the classic DOS development environments many of us grew up with.</p>
      <div><p>The blue editor. The function keys. The compiler messages. The output window.</p><p>Only this time, you're writing Java on a modern Mac.</p><p class="product-proof">And yes, the code actually runs.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
